<title>MEXICO: Improved corn techniques gives Mexico supply hopes.</title>
<headline>Improved corn techniques gives Mexico supply hopes.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new method of growing corn, combining ground control and upgraded planting techniques, could overturn Mexico's perennial problem of being deficient in the nation's number one staple.</p>
<p>The technique has managed to triple production in 33 test plots in the Mexican state of Jalisco to 12 tonnes a hectare from an average of 3.5 tonnes on average harvested in the spring-summer growing cycle in 1994, a regional farming group leader said.</p>
</text>
